A||||6||theogre||Service Notice: 84-87 Rear rotors.||||4||
Z||000000||theogre||04-23-2001||10:14 PM||||I'd heard comments about noises after changing rear rotors on 84-87 cars.... So I kept an eye out for it after changing mine this weekend.<P>sure enough I developed hiddious noise.<P>As Many have found out, it's easy to bend the stone shields and get a noise from the rear brakes, especially when turning corners.<P>This noise was allong that line but one hell of allot worse.<P>The problem is NOT that the shield is bent. That was the first thing I checked.<P>So I pulled the wheel back off.<P>It turns out the inside of the rotor hat is slightly differant than OE rotors. It's just a smidge smaller in diameter.<P>It ends up rubbing the shield next to the hub. It can contact the shield all the way around.<P>DO NOT let this go if you have this happen to you. You can litterally cut thru the shield. Mine had significant wear after only a few miles.<P>The cure is to take a big screw driver or a dull chisle (I used a section cut from an old tire iron.) and bang the shield back. Use the marks left by the rotor as a guide.<P>After doing that I got rid of the noise, At least most of it. I might have to give them another treatment after driving it to work again tomorow but the worst of it is now gone.<P>------------------<BR><I><B>Screamin Yellow Zonkers... If it's Screamin and Yellow, I ain't eatin it.</B></I>||||reg||4
Z||000001||FieroJoe||04-23-2001||10:30 PM||||Very interesting.  I re-did my brakes about a year ago.  I havent ever noticed anything like you describe, possibly just a different brand of rotors you got?<P>Well, I bet it is a very unique noise, metal on metal.  If I ever get it I know what do to now!  <P>------------------<BR>AIM: Fiero87311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto near completion!<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||V8Fiero||04-23-2001||11:09 PM||||Another thing that I found out that will cause that rubbing noise on the brake shield is bad wheel bearings. Rotor/wheel wobbles and rubs.......<P>Not a constant noise but a....scrape/silence....scrape/silence    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>You get the idea....<P>Scott||||reg||1
