Z||000005||84Bill||04-24-2001||08:06 AM||||I have been cussen and swearing for the last two days because of theese things. apparently I bent the driver side shield when swapping engine/cradle units and all I hear when turning corners is screech...screech.... screeech. <P>Any problem with removing them??||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||04-24-2001||07:08 PM||||Bill,,, take the wheel off and see where it's rubbing. If it's the edge of the rotor just bend the sheild back. You should be able to see the contact point easily.<P>It's allot more trouble to remove the shield than bend it or bang it away from the rotor. You have to take out all 3 bolts for the hub. I prefer not to mess with those any more than I have to.<P>V8, <P>My bearings aren't bad. but that's one thing for others to check. (I replaced mine last year.)<P><BR>All,<P>Part of the problem is the shield is easly bent... <P>Another part is that the mounting flange is a bit thicker on some replacement bearings. That moves the shield slightly toward the rotor. Keep in mind there is a certain amount of play built into the hub. This combined with slight diferences in rotor product can be enough to drag the inside of the rotor on the shield. <P>||||reg||1
